From c405d6a098169f32011a928e3770187c19e103de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 10:26:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Stop the bottom sheets fighting the keyboard

Two bugs, one cause: the add-money sheet was being treated like a normal
screen.

Shrinking the container was right for the full screens and wrong here. A
bottom sheet is anchored to the bottom, so shrinking it drags the whole
form downwards into the keyboard it was trying to escape. Worse, on
Android a Modal is its own window and the keyboard height sometimes
reads as zero inside one, so the sheet did not move at all and the
fields simply sat behind the keyboard.

The sheet stays put now, and its scroll content gains room underneath
equal to the keyboard's height. The field being typed into can be
scrolled up into the part still visible, and when the height reads zero
the padding is zero and we are no worse off than before.

Separately: opening "Add money" straight from the search box left that
keyboard standing while the sheet animated up behind it, and the two
arrived half-drawn on top of each other. The sheet brings its own
keyboard when a field is tapped; it should not inherit the last
screen's.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017qsfq3JXWhwEdcaLUroXZy
